        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "CERES",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "INHERITED_FROM",
            "target_entity_instance": "SRB",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "For Rn, we compare against two satellite-based products from Clouds and the Earth's Radiant Energy System (CERES, https://ceres.larc.nasa.gov/) SYN1d Ed4A product38 and Surface Radiation Budget (SRB, https:// eosweb.larc.nasa.gov/project/srb/srb_table) release 3.1. Both products combine diverse atmospheric satellite data extensively with data assimilation, while SRB can be regarded as a precursor to CERES.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MODIS",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "land surface temperature",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "To produce spatio-temporal grids of energy fluxes, the trained machine learning algorithms require only spatio-temporal grids of input data. We used MODIS land products (collection 5; https://lpdaac.usgs.gov/) as input data for FLUXCOM. The MODIS products include daytime and nighttime land surface temperature (LST; MOD11A226), land cover (MCD12Q127), fraction of absorbed photosynthetically active radiation by a canopy (fPAR) (MOD15A228), and bidirectional reflectance distribution function (BRDF)-corrected reflectances (MCD43B429).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
